  "question": {
    "text": "An element <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> crystallises in a body centred cubic unit cell with a cell edge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mi>pm</mi></math>. The density of the element is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The number of atoms present in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of the element is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;(Nearest integer)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "22",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> is body centred cubic, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Let mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;atom of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Edge length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mi>pm</mi></math></p><p>Density&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>300</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p>Atoms of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>180</mn><mrow><mn>81</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>&#8773;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
